name duel-merge-1
timeout 300

# THE ASYMMETRIC DUEL, GEOMETRY 6: THE MERGE — the one place the MiG-29's weapon set is not the
# inferior one, and therefore the mission that has to exist before the campaign may claim the F-16
# dominates. The four BVR geometries all turn on radar reach and Rtr, and on both the MiG is behind by
# construction (2.0x and 1.7x, measured). Inside the merge neither matters: an R-73 is cued off the
# helmet, a GSh-301 round carries 2.7x the energy of an M61A1 round, and the airframe out-turns and
# out-rolls the F-16 (measured corner 420 kt / 24.2 deg/s against 380 / 16.2; roll plant 201 deg/s per
# full deflection against 78.7).
#
# THE SETUP: 8 km apart, head-on, co-altitude, both on `set task bfm` — the close-combat control law
# on both sides, no BVR phase and no long shot. Both start inside every launch zone either side has.
#
# THE MiG ACQUIRES IN THE MERGE (prior round). The pilot switches the N019 to ACM in the fight phase
# (pilot/FBPilot::BfmSelectRadarMode + FBMig29Pilot::BfmRadarModeOrdinal = the broad forward auto-lock
# volume FBMig29Radar::kAcm*, +-37 deg az from T4 7.1 read as azimuth, a +-30 deg vertical band,
# Doppler-exempt like CC), so the auto-lock does the designation the earlier RAD bar could never make.
# The narrow RAD/CC/VS/BORE pencils are unchanged and still used elsewhere (mig29-r73). The F-16 is in
# ACM HUD as before.
#
# AND THE F-16 NOW SURVIVES IT (this round). Its BFM roll law had a PEAK rate cap (90 deg/s) and no bound
# on how LONG a roll may last, while the judge's rule is a SUSTAINED rate (|w| > 60 deg/s for 3 s). At
# 898 kt of closure the line of sight sweeps at up to 543 deg/s -- 34x the corner turn rate -- so the
# commanded lift direction rotated WITH the aircraft, the roll error never closed and the law rolled
# 290 deg in 3.1 s on a 10-20 deg steering error. The same 180 deg that gives the peak cap now also bounds
# the roll flown per kBfmTurnTimeS (doc/pilot.md 5.7.3); the sustained rate follows as cap/2.
#
# READING RULE: exit 2 (CRASH) -- and it is the FULL merge now, decided on the OTHER side and for another
# reason. Measured this round:
#   VIPER (F-16): NO departure. Longest |w| > 60 deg/s stretch 2.9 s -> 0.8 s, roll per 2 s window
#     195.8 -> 110.8 deg, and the run goes from 18.0 s to 232.3 s. lock_s 16.1 -> 28.2.
#   FULCRUM (MiG): RADAR_LOCK t=3.8 (3.32 nm) as before, but now lock_s 14.2 -> 79.4, and it gets the
#     campaign's FIRST WVR employment away -- a 12-round GSh-301 burst at t=195.2, which misses.
#   THE END: the fulcrum descends out of a lost-contact turn and hits the ground at t=232.3 (CFIT). Under
#     the native oracle's real terrain the same event reads ATTITUDE_CONTACT at t=232.2 -- one event, two
#     elevation sources.
# WHAT THIS RUN NOW MEASURES, and it is NOT the weapon thesis: the viper spends 190.1 of 232.3 s with
# bfm_rng = -1, the fulcrum 143.2 s, 133.6 s both at once. After the first pass neither ACM box
# re-acquires, the fight becomes two blind sustained turns, both jets sink (the viper settles at 474 m
# AGL, below its own 2000 ft BFM floor) and the MiG loses that race. So the R-73/GSh-301 thesis stays untested for a FOURTH reason, and it is the honest one: the
# pilots cannot hold each other in a knife fight. The blocker is no longer a control law on either side --
# it is close-combat re-acquisition plus the BFM floor. doc/duels.md D1, doc/pilot.md gaps 2.9 + 2.8.

unit viper
  team friendly
  module f16
  spawn 46.90000 6.95000 5000 90.0 380
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set datalink off
  set fcr_mode acm_hud                      # auto-locks the nearest firm track: no thumb needed
  set fcr_range_nm 10
  set rwr on
  set store 3 aim9
  set store 7 aim9
  set cmds_mode man
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task bfm
  wp 46.90000 7.20000 5000 380
  objective kill unit fulcrum
  objective survive

unit fulcrum
  team hostile
  module mig29
  spawn 46.90000 7.05500 5000 270.0 380
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set n019_mode rad                         # BVR default; the BFM pilot switches to ACM in the fight
  set n019_range_nm 10
  set n019_emission illum
  set rwr on
  set store 3 r73
  set store 4 r73
  set cmds_mode man                          # the MiG can now defend too (BVP-30-26, this round)
  set cmds_chaff 30
  set cmds_flare 30
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task bfm
  wp 46.90000 6.80000 5000 380
  objective kill unit viper
  objective survive
